+# Hotbar: Figma to Roblox notes
+
+Source: `design/figma/hotbar.json`, from the Figma file "Block Builder - UI", version
+2208815566419836712 (last modified 2026-11-02). Node 31:100 is the HUD / Desktop frame (1920 x 1080)
+and node 31:2 is the Hotbar Slot component set. The export had no screenshot, so everything here
+comes from the node data alone. Nobody has compared it with the Figma canvas yet.
+
+Implementation: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Hotbar.luau`.
+
+## What matches the design
+
+These come straight from the JSON. The frame is 1080 tall, the same as `Screen.ReferenceHeight`,
+so Figma pixels map 1:1 to offsets.
+
+- Bar: 732 x 84, 10 px padding, 8 px between slots, corner radius 14, fill `#0E1020`, 24 px above
+  the bottom of the screen.
+- Slots: 64 x 64, corner radius 12. Fills are Default `#262B45`, Hover `#313858` and Pressed
+  `#1D2136`.
+- Swatch: 40 x 40, inset 12, corner radius 8, filled with the block's color.
+- Key badge: an 18 x 18 circle at (4, 4), black at 55%, with Builder Sans Bold 12 in white.
+- Selected slot: a 3 px stroke outside the tile with a left-to-right gradient from `#FFD25A` to
+  `#FF801A`. This is a `UIStroke` (Border mode, which draws outside the edge) with a `UIGradient`.
+- Selected name: 22 px, white, 28 px tall, 8 px above the bar. Its outline is 2 px black at 60%.
+- Pressed variant: the tile shrinks to 60 x 60, the swatch to 36 x 36 and the badge moves to
+  (3, 3), as in the design. The button itself stays 64 x 64, so neighboring slots don't move.
+
+## What Roblox can't do exactly, and what's used instead
+
+| Design | Problem in Roblox | Used instead |
+|---|---|---|
+| Selected name font is **Gilroy ExtraBold** (800) | Gilroy isn't a Roblox font. Custom fonts can't be uploaded. | **Builder Sans ExtraBold**, the same family as the key labels. The letters will be shaped differently and the width will change a little. To get closer, the designer can pick from Roblox's font list (Montserrat ExtraBold is the nearest geometric sans). |
+| Selected name **letter spacing −0.5 px** | `TextLabel` has no letter-spacing property. | Default spacing, so the text is slightly wider than in the mock. |
+| Selected name outline is drawn **OUTSIDE** the glyphs | `UIStroke` on text (Contextual mode) can't be placed inside or outside like Figma's option. | `UIStroke` with Thickness 2, black, Transparency 0.4. On screen the outline may look a little heavier or lighter than Figma's. |
+| Bar **opacity 0.8** on the whole layer | Roblox has no layer opacity on a plain Frame. Setting 80% transparency on each element separately isn't the same, because the bar would show through the slots and the slots through the swatches. | The bar is a **`CanvasGroup`** with `GroupTransparency = 0.2`, which composites it like Figma does. Costs: a CanvasGroup renders to a texture, which uses some GPU memory. It re-renders when anything inside changes, such as the selection or hover. Its contents can look slightly soft on some devices. If that's a problem, switch to a Frame and give each element its own transparency. |
+| Bar stroke on the **top edge only** (`individualStrokeWeights` top 2, others 0), drawn inside, white at 12% | `UIStroke` always strokes every side, and Border mode draws outside the edge. A CanvasGroup would clip anything outside anyway. | A 2 px Frame, white at 88% transparency, along the top of the bar. It's 28 px shorter than the bar (14 px off each end), so it stops where the rounded corners begin. Figma's stroke continues a short way around the corners and thins out; this line doesn't. |
+| **Corner smoothing 0.6** on slots (iOS-style squircle) | `UICorner` only makes circular arcs. | Plain `UICorner` with a 12 px radius. The corners are a little sharper where the curve meets the straight edge. |
+| **Hover** state | Touch screens have no hover. | Comes from `GuiButton.GuiState` (Idle / Hover / Press), so it shows with a mouse only. Touch shows Default and Pressed. `AutoButtonColor` is off so Roblox's own tint doesn't stack on top. |
+| No variant for **Selected + Hover / Pressed** | The component set has Selected, Hover and Pressed, but no combination of them. | A selected slot still changes fill and size on hover and press, and keeps its gradient stroke. The designer may want to confirm this. |
+| Selected name **auto-width** (`WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT`) | Works in Roblox but isn't needed here. | A fixed 240 x 28 label with centered text, as before. All block names fit. |
+
+## Design values not used
+
+- Every swatch in the export has the Brick color (`#A34B3C`). The component description says the
+  swatch fill comes from the game, so each slot uses `BlockTypes` colors.
+- In the game, Window and Ice blocks are partly transparent. The design doesn't show that, so their
+  swatches stay opaque, the same as before the reskin.
+- The `Show Key` property is true on every instance, so badges are always shown.
+- The frame is the desktop layout only. No mobile frame was exported, so phones get the same layout
+  at the authored size (`Screen.uiScale` never goes below 1). The new bar is 732 px wide, up from 630 px,
+  so it's more likely to run off the edge on a phone held upright. That needs a check on a device.
